  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...An upper ridge and Bermuda high pressure \nremains centered off the coast today. Most guidance keeps dry\nconditions to day with broad subsidence and lack of forcing,\nhowever cannot completely rule out an isolated shower or\nthunderstorm along the sea breeze this afternoon. The ridge \nbecomes suppressed tonight into Sunday as shortwave energy \npushes across the mid-Atlantic with more of a zonal pattern \ndeveloping next week with a series of shortwave troughs pushing \nacross the area. Precip chances will be near climo each day with\nscattered showers and thunderstorms with best chances through \npeak heating, but will also depend of timing of individual\nshortwave troughs. The severe threat appears minimal through\nmuch of the period with limited shear, though somewhat better\nshear develops toward the middle of next week. \n\nHot temperatures continue into next week as well with highs in \nthe lower 90s inland through the weekend, then warming in to the\nmid 90s next week. Temps generally in the mid to upper 80s \nalong the coast. The probabilities for Major Heat Risk increase \nto around 50-80% Monday through Thursday with highest probs on \nTuesday and Wednesday.",
